WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.279 --> 00:00:05.210
Here we are again with the Anom-O-Tron 6000,
our state-of-the-art simulation computer that

00:00:05.210 --> 00:00:10.590
helps us create hyper-accurate simulations
of some of the world’s most bizarre scenarios.

00:00:10.590 --> 00:00:17.449
Whether it’s 096 Vs Siren Head, Able Vs
Chainsaw Man, or now, perhaps our most ridiculous

00:00:17.449 --> 00:00:25.550
match-up yet: SCP-035, the diabolical Possessive
Mask, Vs The Mask, the popular Jim Carrey

00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:29.269
character based on the hyper-violent comic
book of the same name.

00:00:29.269 --> 00:00:30.269
So…

00:00:30.269 --> 00:00:31.830
What the heck are we waiting for?

00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:35.390
Let’s crank up the machine and see what
the results are.

00:00:35.390 --> 00:00:36.940
Somebody stop me!

00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:40.070
“Okay, so what have we got on intake today?”

00:00:40.070 --> 00:00:43.980
Researcher Werb asked, a tone of boredom hanging
off his every word.

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:49.280
“Possible anomalous entity,” his compatriot
Doctor Mahnke replied, sipping his coffee,

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:50.540
sounding equally as unenthused.

00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:52.030
“Caucasian male, early thirties.

00:00:52.030 --> 00:00:57.519
A team of our agents picked him up in…”
the Foundation doctor checked his notes.

00:00:57.519 --> 00:01:03.390
“Some place called ‘Edge City’, real
appealing tourist spot,” he added sarcastically.

00:01:03.390 --> 00:01:05.619
“What’s so anomalous about him?”

00:01:05.619 --> 00:01:09.680
Werb questioned as his eyes lazily scanned
over a file Mahnke had handed him.

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:12.010
“Says here he’s just an ordinary bank
teller.

00:01:12.010 --> 00:01:15.590
There’s one prior arrest on his record,
but the charges were dropped later on.

00:01:15.590 --> 00:01:17.240
This guy’s a nobody.”

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:21.630
“Apparently, he was in possession of an
anomalous artifact,” came the doctor’s

00:01:21.630 --> 00:01:22.630
reply.

00:01:22.630 --> 00:01:25.040
He looked through the one-way glass into the
interrogation room.

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:31.000
Sat at the table wearing a matching pair of
hideous pajamas was a wiry, brown-haired man.

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:32.340
“What was it?”

00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:35.591
Researcher Werb asked, not bothering to check
the file.

00:01:35.591 --> 00:01:37.210
“A mask apparently,” Mahnke replied.

00:01:37.210 --> 00:01:41.119
“This think can form a symbiotic connection
with whoever wears it.

00:01:41.119 --> 00:01:45.070
This guy’s had it for a while, it causes
him to undergo a dramatic intensification

00:01:45.070 --> 00:01:50.680
of his personality when he puts it on, as
well as granting him some… unusual abilities.”

00:01:50.680 --> 00:01:53.960
“Hold on, aren’t you just describing SCP-035?”

00:01:53.960 --> 00:01:55.409
Werb said, looking confused.

00:01:55.409 --> 00:01:56.409
“Nope.”

00:01:56.409 --> 00:01:59.080
The doctor responded by handing him a clear
evidence bag.

00:01:59.080 --> 00:02:04.049
In it was a simple wooden mask, a dull, dark
greenish tint to the object.

00:02:04.049 --> 00:02:09.250
It looked to be almost Viking in its design,
with three holes on its surface; one for the

00:02:09.250 --> 00:02:11.280
mouth and two for the eyes.

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:17.040
It was hard to deny, it was completely different
from the white porcelain of SCP-035.

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:19.610
“What’s this guy’s name again?”

00:02:19.610 --> 00:02:23.690
Werb sighed, looking at the scruffy, pajama-clad
man waiting for them.

00:02:23.690 --> 00:02:25.500
“Ipkiss,” his colleague replied.

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:26.970
“Stanley Ipkiss.”

00:02:26.970 --> 00:02:33.030
Meanwhile, locked up tight in a hermetically
sealed glass case, was another anomalous mask.

00:02:33.030 --> 00:02:38.400
SCP-035 was kept under lock and key by the
Foundation, guarded constantly by a pair of

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:40.349
armed security officers.

00:02:40.349 --> 00:02:44.069
One of them, Officer Riegert, had noticed
something seemed strange about the infamous

00:02:44.069 --> 00:02:48.310
Possessive Mask today; or stranger than usual
anyway.

00:02:48.310 --> 00:02:53.480
SCP-035 was known to compel people to wear
it if they were close enough, often through

00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:55.170
subtle, psychic whispers.

00:02:55.170 --> 00:02:57.730
But today, it seemed…

00:02:57.730 --> 00:03:02.670
restless, almost agitated, like it found something
nearby to be intensely annoying.

00:03:02.670 --> 00:03:07.280
“I already told you everything I know,”
Stanley Ipkiss sighed exhaustedly.

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:11.459
He’d been dragged out of bed at the crack
of dawn by strange agents and was now being

00:03:11.459 --> 00:03:15.909
interrogated about what he knew of the wooden
Mask he’d come across floating in the river

00:03:15.909 --> 00:03:17.220
one fateful night.

00:03:17.220 --> 00:03:21.830
“I don’t know where it came from; I swear,
I didn’t even realize I still had it!

00:03:21.830 --> 00:03:25.530
We threw it back in the river, but my dog
must’ve swum out and fetched it,” Stanley

00:03:25.530 --> 00:03:26.530
explained.

00:03:26.530 --> 00:03:28.510
“You have no idea what this thing is?

00:03:28.510 --> 00:03:31.500
Not even from any firsthand experience, Mr.
Ipkiss?”

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:33.390
Doctor Mahnke asked, holding the mask up.

00:03:33.390 --> 00:03:38.460
“Look, I did take it to a psychologist who
told me it might be Scandinavian, a representation

00:03:38.460 --> 00:03:42.269
of some Norse night god, Loki, I think,”
he answered.

00:03:42.269 --> 00:03:47.290
“We’re not interested in this mask as
a historical art piece,” Researcher Werb

00:03:47.290 --> 00:03:48.290
retorted.

00:03:48.290 --> 00:03:50.560
“Tell us what happens when you put it on.”

00:03:50.560 --> 00:03:54.720
Stanley paused for a moment, clearly aware
he was in real trouble, but nervous about

00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:57.769
coughing up the details to his shady captors.

00:03:57.769 --> 00:04:00.220
With a sigh, he decided it was best to confess.

00:04:00.220 --> 00:04:05.629
“I don’t know how it works, but whenever
you put it on it’s like it brings your deepest

00:04:05.629 --> 00:04:06.629
desires to life.

00:04:06.629 --> 00:04:09.470
When I wear that mask, I can do anything…

00:04:09.470 --> 00:04:12.879
be anything,” he described, remembering
a key detail.

00:04:12.879 --> 00:04:15.069
“But it only works at night.”

00:04:15.069 --> 00:04:19.889
Doctor Mahnke and Researcher Werb exchanged
looks, uncertain if Ipkiss was just a lunatic

00:04:19.889 --> 00:04:22.470
or if there was truth to what he was telling
them.

00:04:22.470 --> 00:04:25.280
“Assemble a security team,” Mahnke sighed.

00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:28.730
“We’ll arrange a safe environment for
you tonight, Mr Ipkiss.”

00:04:28.730 --> 00:04:32.820
Elsewhere in the facility, Riegert and his
fellow Security Officer, Doughan, were watching

00:04:32.820 --> 00:04:35.530
over SCP-035 with growing concern.

00:04:35.530 --> 00:04:38.010
“What do you reckon has this thing so agitated?”

00:04:38.010 --> 00:04:39.700
Doughan wondered aloud.

00:04:39.700 --> 00:04:41.690
“Who knows,” Riegert sighed.

00:04:41.690 --> 00:04:45.310
“I’ve already reported to Command, told
them 035’s in a mood.

00:04:45.310 --> 00:04:47.260
They said to proceed as normal.”

00:04:47.260 --> 00:04:51.190
Suddenly, as the words left his mouth, Officer
Riegert felt strange.

00:04:51.190 --> 00:04:55.110
It was like he had been hooked by an overwhelming
urge to put the Possessive Mask on, staring

00:04:55.110 --> 00:04:56.110
at its exaggerated white porcelain face, locked
in a tragedy frown.

00:04:56.110 --> 00:05:00.750
He barely noticed he had reached to unlock
the door sealing the area where SCP-035 was

00:05:00.750 --> 00:05:05.960
contained in its case, and as he stepped through,
Officer Doughan’s pleas for him to stop

00:05:05.960 --> 00:05:07.550
barely registered.

00:05:07.550 --> 00:05:12.479
The other officer tried in vain to pull Riegert
back as he walked towards the Possessive Mask,

00:05:12.479 --> 00:05:17.569
only to feel his co-worker grip his shirt
and swing him face-first over and over again

00:05:17.569 --> 00:05:20.710
into the glass case containing the anomalous
object.

00:05:20.710 --> 00:05:25.121
His body going completely limp after being
used to break the glass, Riegert dropped Doughan

00:05:25.121 --> 00:05:30.680
to the floor, too lost in his trance-like
state to realize he’d just killed a fellow

00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:32.410
Foundation security officer.

00:05:32.410 --> 00:05:38.590
He was too focused on SCP-035, as he lifted
it up and placed it over his face.

00:05:38.590 --> 00:05:43.330
Meanwhile, Stanley Ipkiss had been brought
to a testing area, a team of security officers

00:05:43.330 --> 00:05:44.759
standing around him.

00:05:44.759 --> 00:05:48.720
The fact that they were all armed did little
to ease Stanley’s nerves.

00:05:48.720 --> 00:05:52.570
Doctor Mahnke strode up to him, pulling the
green wooden mask out of the airtight bag

00:05:52.570 --> 00:05:55.400
it had been sealed in, and handed it to Stanley.

00:05:55.400 --> 00:05:59.190
“No funny business, Mr. Ipkiss,” the doctor
warned.

00:05:59.190 --> 00:06:02.470
“I really can’t promise that,” Stanley
replied.

00:06:02.470 --> 00:06:07.280
He looked at the mask in his hands, noticing
a green shimmer over the reverse side of it.

00:06:07.280 --> 00:06:11.280
As much as he had gladly given it up, part
of him had missed wearing it.

00:06:11.280 --> 00:06:15.430
He could already hear the low rumbling of
thunder outside as he lifted it towards his

00:06:15.430 --> 00:06:19.740
face, feeling it almost leap out of his hands
and latch itself onto him.

00:06:19.740 --> 00:06:24.220
The green mask eagerly became attached to
Stanley, the surface of it spreading out from

00:06:24.220 --> 00:06:27.949
where it covered his face to wrap around his
entire head.

00:06:27.949 --> 00:06:31.841
Around him, the guards cautiously stepped
back as they watched Stanley convulsing and

00:06:31.841 --> 00:06:36.099
writhing about the place uncontrollably like
a man possessed.

00:06:36.099 --> 00:06:40.641
Both Researcher Weld and Doctor Mahnke looked
at one another in wordless disbelief, before

00:06:40.641 --> 00:06:44.360
turning back to the scene unfolding before
their eyes.

00:06:44.360 --> 00:06:48.340
The booming noise of thunder and cracks of
lightning rang out, despite this all taking

00:06:48.340 --> 00:06:53.560
place indoors, as Stanley Ipkiss vanished
in the center of a miniature tornado that

00:06:53.560 --> 00:06:57.879
spun wildly around the testing area, before
slowing to a halt.

00:06:57.879 --> 00:07:03.729
In its place stood a maniacal, wide-eyed figure,
dressed in a garish yellow zoot suit and wearing

00:07:03.729 --> 00:07:06.760
an enormous toothed grin on his bright green
face.

00:07:06.760 --> 00:07:08.830
“How do, fellas?”

00:07:08.830 --> 00:07:13.450
the Mask bombastically hooted at the guards
Having been trained to deal with absurd anomalies

00:07:13.450 --> 00:07:17.990
aplenty, the security team all defensively
raised their weapons out of a mix of instinct

00:07:17.990 --> 00:07:19.210
and confusion.

00:07:19.210 --> 00:07:24.090
“Yeesh, rough crowd,” the green-faced
lunatic stated to nobody; it looked like he

00:07:24.090 --> 00:07:28.680
had turned aside, as if addressing some invisible
audience.

00:07:28.680 --> 00:07:33.850
Outstretching both arms and one leg, the Mask
instantly zipped off, hurling around the room

00:07:33.850 --> 00:07:38.660
in a whirlwind of absurdity, in the style
of an old Tex Avery cartoon.

00:07:38.660 --> 00:07:43.250
The spinning, cackling combination of Stanley
Ipkiss and the magical mask weaved in between

00:07:43.250 --> 00:07:48.220
the Foundation guards, all of whom tried in
vain to restrain him until he disappeared

00:07:48.220 --> 00:07:49.300
out of the door.

00:07:49.300 --> 00:07:50.610
“After him!”

00:07:50.610 --> 00:07:52.790
Doctor Mahnke yelled with urgency in his voice.

00:07:52.790 --> 00:07:56.889
The guards all turned to run after the Mask,
only for each one of them to trip over and

00:07:56.889 --> 00:08:02.169
land face-first on the floor of the testing
area, as if something had tied them all up

00:08:02.169 --> 00:08:03.169
by their ankles.

00:08:03.169 --> 00:08:07.940
It was only as the security officers all struggled
back up to their feet that they noticed their

00:08:07.940 --> 00:08:14.639
pants had been yanked down, leaving the Foundation’s
finest somewhat embarrassed, to say the least.

00:08:14.639 --> 00:08:19.610
Outside the testing area, Stanley – or rather,
The Mask – had already closed the door behind

00:08:19.610 --> 00:08:20.610
him.

00:08:20.610 --> 00:08:25.470
Out of nowhere, he produced a series of wooden
planks and began hammering them into the doorframe,

00:08:25.470 --> 00:08:29.310
boarding it up before speedily adding chains
and padlocks to the mix.

00:08:29.310 --> 00:08:35.260
Sighing and exaggeratedly wiping sweat from
his brow, he turned around… only to be met

00:08:35.260 --> 00:08:39.820
with the sight of even more SCP Foundation
guards lying in wait, their guns all trained

00:08:39.820 --> 00:08:40.820
on him.

00:08:40.820 --> 00:08:44.589
The Mask gave a scream of pure terror that
briefly sent his skull popping out of his

00:08:44.589 --> 00:08:49.209
head, and his eyes shooting out of his skull,
before everything zipped right back into its

00:08:49.209 --> 00:08:50.600
original place.

00:08:50.600 --> 00:08:54.589
His eyes darted around at the faces of the
Foundation security, wondering how he was

00:08:54.589 --> 00:08:56.240
going to get out of this one.

00:08:56.240 --> 00:09:00.649
“Gee, this all seems familiar,” he said,
either to himself or his audience.

00:09:00.649 --> 00:09:02.790
“Well, if it ain’t broken: hit it!”

00:09:02.790 --> 00:09:06.890
In the blink of an eye, the Mask’s bright
yellow outfit had transformed, replaced by

00:09:06.890 --> 00:09:12.089
a silk blue rumba shirt with ruffled sleeves,
white pants and a wide-brimmed black hat.

00:09:12.089 --> 00:09:16.310
As they watched him, stood at the ready, a
few of the guards noticed the sound of…

00:09:16.310 --> 00:09:17.310
music?

00:09:17.310 --> 00:09:20.820
Not one of them could tell where it was coming
from, nor could they help starting to tap

00:09:20.820 --> 00:09:25.960
their feet or bob their heads to the rhythm
of the Cuban Pete rumba.

00:09:25.960 --> 00:09:30.040
The entire security team quickly erupted into
a full-blown dance number that anyone who

00:09:30.040 --> 00:09:35.440
saw it couldn’t resist joining, all led
by the Mask, wildly waving maracas in the

00:09:35.440 --> 00:09:36.970
air and singing.

00:09:36.970 --> 00:09:40.280
Elsewhere in the facilty, Officer Riegert
was beginning to melt.

00:09:40.280 --> 00:09:45.670
He still had SCP-035 covering his face, the
frown of the Possessive Mask conveying the

00:09:45.670 --> 00:09:48.130
entity’s sheer discontent.

00:09:48.130 --> 00:09:53.050
The black ooze secreting from its porcelain
surface had the unfortunate effect of corroding

00:09:53.050 --> 00:09:59.370
and melting down anyone that wore it, dissolving
them entirely after a short period of time.

00:09:59.370 --> 00:10:04.590
Determined, SCP-035 pushed on, piloting its
host towards a storage room.

00:10:04.590 --> 00:10:09.950
If it remembered correctly, the SCP Foundation
had stored a number of temporary hosts for

00:10:09.950 --> 00:10:14.769
it, mannequins that, while not human, had
enough of a humanoid shape for the Possessive

00:10:14.769 --> 00:10:16.410
Mask to use.

00:10:16.410 --> 00:10:20.649
Of course, after all its attempts to escape,
the Foundation had rescinded its privilege

00:10:20.649 --> 00:10:26.210
to be granted new hosts… not that they could
stop it from taking them by force.

00:10:26.210 --> 00:10:31.950
Using the last of Officer Riegert’s dwindling
strength, SCP-035 barged its way into the

00:10:31.950 --> 00:10:32.950
storeroom.

00:10:32.950 --> 00:10:36.670
Sure enough, waiting there for it was a row
of discarded mannequins.

00:10:36.670 --> 00:10:40.800
Lifting Riegert’s hands before they had
fully melted away, the Possessive Mask used

00:10:40.800 --> 00:10:43.670
him to place itself on a new body.

00:10:43.670 --> 00:10:48.410
Elsewhere, not too far away in the Foundation
facility, a conga line of security officers

00:10:48.410 --> 00:10:53.380
and research personnel was parading through
the corridors, all happily dancing and jiving

00:10:53.380 --> 00:10:58.810
to the music despite still no one being able
to figure out where it was coming from.

00:10:58.810 --> 00:11:03.040
Dashing away from his spot at the front of
the line, the Mask zipped around a corner,

00:11:03.040 --> 00:11:06.420
his clothes having changed back into his signature
brightly-colored zoot suit.

00:11:06.420 --> 00:11:11.430
“Never say no to a party!” he exclaimed,
after having danced his way to freedom.

00:11:11.430 --> 00:11:15.360
The sound of something shuffling closer quickly
caught the Mask’s attention.

00:11:15.360 --> 00:11:20.530
He turned around to find himself standing
green face to porcelain face with SCP-035.

00:11:20.530 --> 00:11:26.709
“You…” the masked mannequin raised a
hollow arm, pointing a finger from its host

00:11:26.709 --> 00:11:27.709
at Stanley.

00:11:27.709 --> 00:11:30.839
“You bear the God of Mischief’s carving!

00:11:30.839 --> 00:11:33.440
I could sense its presence since you arrived!”

00:11:33.440 --> 00:11:34.850
“Stealing my look?

00:11:34.850 --> 00:11:36.290
Nobody likes a copycat, fella!”

00:11:36.290 --> 00:11:37.290
the Mask replied.

00:11:37.290 --> 00:11:42.020
“Although imitation is the sincerest form
of flattery – and that’s how Jim Carrey’s

00:11:42.020 --> 00:11:46.480
career started!” he added, exploding with
raucous laughter.

00:11:46.480 --> 00:11:48.459
“Cease your prattling!”

00:11:48.459 --> 00:11:51.110
SCP-035 hissed with spite.

00:11:51.110 --> 00:11:52.779
“Say, perhaps we’re related?”

00:11:52.779 --> 00:11:54.600
the Mask ignored it.

00:11:54.600 --> 00:11:55.930
“We could be long-lost family!

00:11:55.930 --> 00:11:58.149
You know, I always wanted kids of my own.

00:11:58.149 --> 00:12:03.000
Son of the Mask, has a nice ring to it, right?”
he paused, once again turning to his unseen

00:12:03.000 --> 00:12:04.000
audience.

00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:07.700
“On second thoughts, maybe not.”

00:12:07.700 --> 00:12:11.769
The SCP-035-controlled mannequin leapt forward,
gripping the Mask’s arm, causing him to

00:12:11.769 --> 00:12:13.760
scream in shock at the advance.

00:12:13.760 --> 00:12:18.290
His eye’s bulged out of their sockets, zooming
in on the corrosive black secretions oozing

00:12:18.290 --> 00:12:19.600
from SCP-035.

00:12:19.600 --> 00:12:25.560
The mannequin’s other hand started reaching
upwards, gripping his oversized green head,

00:12:25.560 --> 00:12:29.449
as if it was trying to lift the mask right
off of Stanley’s face.

00:12:29.449 --> 00:12:34.389
Zooming away again, he sped down the nearest
corridor, his arm stretching behind him, still

00:12:34.389 --> 00:12:37.310
clamped in SCP-035’s grip.

00:12:37.310 --> 00:12:41.769
Coming to a screeching halt with the comical
sound of car brakes, the Mask wobbled his

00:12:41.769 --> 00:12:43.220
outstretched arm.

00:12:43.220 --> 00:12:48.610
A ripple traveled all the way along the elongated
limb, as if it was made of elastic.

00:12:48.610 --> 00:12:52.970
His wrist still being held by the mannequin
sporting the Possessive Mask, the force of

00:12:52.970 --> 00:12:59.019
the flailing, rubbery arm was so great that
it flung SCP-035’s host body around, sending

00:12:59.019 --> 00:13:03.730
it heat-first up into the ceiling, then plummeting
back down to the ground.

00:13:03.730 --> 00:13:08.480
Its grip loosened, allowing the Mask to reel
back his stretchy arm, although it didn’t

00:13:08.480 --> 00:13:10.540
return to normal length right away.

00:13:10.540 --> 00:13:15.430
His own hand pinged back and hit him in the
face, only to start urgently trying to communicate

00:13:15.430 --> 00:13:16.430
of its own accord.

00:13:16.430 --> 00:13:17.670
“What’s that, boy?”

00:13:17.670 --> 00:13:21.060
the Mask said to his hand as it started performing
a series of signals.

00:13:21.060 --> 00:13:22.690
“Little Timmy’s stuck down a well?

00:13:22.690 --> 00:13:23.910
You’d like Friday night’s off?

00:13:23.910 --> 00:13:27.279
There’s a two-bit chump wearing another
mask walking menacingly down the hall towards

00:13:27.279 --> 00:13:28.279
us?”

00:13:28.279 --> 00:13:32.480
The hand suddenly turned the Mask’s head
to look in the right direction; sure enough,

00:13:32.480 --> 00:13:36.899
SCP-035 was using the mannequin to walk menacing
down the hall towards him.

00:13:36.899 --> 00:13:41.320
His elongated arm quickly returned to its
normal size, as the green-faced lunatic took

00:13:41.320 --> 00:13:44.600
a quick draw stance, facing his oncoming adversary.

00:13:44.600 --> 00:13:50.310
“Now, you have to ask yourself one question,”
he sneered, doing a fairly convincing impression

00:13:50.310 --> 00:13:51.790
of a green Clint Eastwood.

00:13:51.790 --> 00:13:54.070
“Do I feel lucky?”

00:13:54.070 --> 00:13:57.160
With a sweep of his hand, the Mask had drawn
an enormous weapon.

00:13:57.160 --> 00:14:01.339
The thing was a gigantic mass of different
artillery, clicking and whirring.

00:14:01.339 --> 00:14:06.310
There were barrels on top of barrels, rockets,
and other explosives locking into place.

00:14:06.310 --> 00:14:08.350
“Do I feel lucky?”

00:14:08.350 --> 00:14:09.490
the Mask continued.

00:14:09.490 --> 00:14:12.250
“Well, do ya, punk?”

00:14:12.250 --> 00:14:16.590
SCP-035 did nothing to slow its advance, so
the Mask pulled the trigger.

00:14:16.590 --> 00:14:20.579
Every one of his weapon’s various components
spat out a tiny flag with the word ‘bang’

00:14:20.579 --> 00:14:21.579
written on it.

00:14:21.579 --> 00:14:24.620
“Ah, a performance issue,” he said, doing
his aside once again.

00:14:24.620 --> 00:14:27.970
“Not that I’m overcompensating for anything.”

00:14:27.970 --> 00:14:34.329
Clearly growing agitated, piloting its host,
SCP-035 started charging towards the Mask.

00:14:34.329 --> 00:14:39.269
Immediately, he spun around, becoming a tornado
of hyperactivity and whooping noises as he

00:14:39.269 --> 00:14:41.449
sped down the adjacent corridor.

00:14:41.449 --> 00:14:45.880
The Possessive Mask staggered after him, the
ooze leaking from the porcelain anomaly was

00:14:45.880 --> 00:14:50.870
dripping onto the mannequin wearing it, causing
the plastic to be melted away, exposing the

00:14:50.870 --> 00:14:52.779
flimsy metal skeleton beneath.

00:14:52.779 --> 00:14:57.710
It knew it had to merge with a new host, find
something else to corrupt.

00:14:57.710 --> 00:15:03.149
SCP-035 chased after the cartoonish troublemaker,
knowing that if it could catch him, he’d

00:15:03.149 --> 00:15:07.930
be able to survive merging with it; his body,
while wearing the other mask, barely obeyed

00:15:07.930 --> 00:15:13.410
the laws of physics, making him invulnerable
to damage, and possibly even the corrosive

00:15:13.410 --> 00:15:16.269
substance oozing from the Possessive Mask.

00:15:16.269 --> 00:15:20.880
As if those weren’t enough reasons, his
powers seemed virtually limitless; combined

00:15:20.880 --> 00:15:26.420
with the green-headed lunatic, SCP-035 could
do anything.

00:15:26.420 --> 00:15:31.480
Reaching a stop at the end of another corridor,
the Mask spun around, wearing a comically-undersized

00:15:31.480 --> 00:15:32.649
baseball uniform.

00:15:32.649 --> 00:15:37.069
He reached into his pocket and produced an
oversized baseball bat, then proceeded to

00:15:37.069 --> 00:15:40.990
start hurling baseballs into the air and swatting
them as hard as he could.

00:15:40.990 --> 00:15:45.819
As the Mask increased the speed of his swings,
a volley of hard, cork baseballs were fired

00:15:45.819 --> 00:15:50.490
down the corridor like a barrage of bullets,
ricocheting off the walls and hitting the

00:15:50.490 --> 00:15:53.310
oncoming SCP-035.

00:15:53.310 --> 00:15:58.110
Each one struck its target, reeling the mannequin
but doing little much else to stop it getting

00:15:58.110 --> 00:16:00.959
closer and closer until…

00:16:00.959 --> 00:16:06.639
With an almighty swing, the Mask brought his
bat crashing into SCP-035 with enough force

00:16:06.639 --> 00:16:11.390
to send the Possessive Mask and its host careening
down the corridor.

00:16:11.390 --> 00:16:16.000
It sailed through the air, bursting through
a wall, then flew into a research lab, tearing

00:16:16.000 --> 00:16:18.839
a huge hole in the next wall as it kept going.

00:16:18.839 --> 00:16:23.180
Finally, it came crashing out of one last
wall; the outer wall of the facility, and

00:16:23.180 --> 00:16:26.180
dropped multiple stories to the ground outside.

00:16:26.180 --> 00:16:31.779
Changing costumes back to his classic suit
and dashing after SCP-035, the Mask passed

00:16:31.779 --> 00:16:36.300
through all the holes his adversary had left
in the multiple walls it had crashed into.

00:16:36.300 --> 00:16:41.040
He screeched to a halt again and paused after
getting through the outer wall, only to realize

00:16:41.040 --> 00:16:46.310
after a moment that he was hovering in mid-air,
not standing on anything.

00:16:46.310 --> 00:16:50.649
Reaching into his suit pocket, the Mask pulled
out a sign on a stick, with a single word

00:16:50.649 --> 00:16:52.620
written on it: ‘yikes’.

00:16:52.620 --> 00:16:57.269
He plummeted down to ground level, landing
with such an immense crash that his body cracked

00:16:57.269 --> 00:16:58.790
into the asphalt below.

00:16:58.790 --> 00:17:03.860
It left a perfect outline of him imprinted
in the ground, causing the Mask to go completely

00:17:03.860 --> 00:17:06.039
pancake-flat head to toe.

00:17:06.039 --> 00:17:09.390
Suddenly, before he could peel himself up
off the ground and go back to being three-dimensional,

00:17:09.390 --> 00:17:15.209
SCP-035 staggered to its host’s feet, and
pinned the Mask down.

00:17:15.209 --> 00:17:16.209
“Finally!”

00:17:16.209 --> 00:17:17.209
it growled.

00:17:17.209 --> 00:17:19.140
“I’ve caught you!

00:17:19.140 --> 00:17:20.449
I’ve won!

00:17:20.449 --> 00:17:25.520
Your power is mine, once I’ve combined with
you I will be able to ravage this world.

00:17:25.520 --> 00:17:30.320
I’m going to fuse to your face, then I’ll
start with decimating those wretches that

00:17:30.320 --> 00:17:37.220
imprisoned me, the Foundation will fall and
then so will the rest of their precious world.”

00:17:37.220 --> 00:17:42.330
Forcefully, the mannequin’s hand wrenched
the Mask off the ground, but as SCP-035 turned

00:17:42.330 --> 00:17:44.760
to look at what it had hoped to be its next
host…

00:17:44.760 --> 00:17:49.330
well, let’s say the tragedy frown carved
into its porcelain face had never been more

00:17:49.330 --> 00:17:50.330
appropriate.

00:17:50.330 --> 00:17:55.020
It wasn’t holding the Mask, it was holding
a life-size cardboard cut-out, a photo of

00:17:55.020 --> 00:17:57.820
the Mask grinning out from one side.

00:17:57.820 --> 00:18:02.150
Enraged, the Possessive Mask tore the decoy
in half with its mannequin’s hands.

00:18:02.150 --> 00:18:05.429
“Hey, Pachuco,” said a cartoonish voice
from right behind it.

00:18:05.429 --> 00:18:06.850
“Did you miss me?”

00:18:06.850 --> 00:18:11.549
The Mask had reappeared, for real this time,
grinning with his huge teeth, clearly getting

00:18:11.549 --> 00:18:14.460
a kick out of having somebody to torment.

00:18:14.460 --> 00:18:19.980
SCP-035, on the other hand, had been getting
increasingly irritated by all the wacky cartoon

00:18:19.980 --> 00:18:20.980
antics.

00:18:20.980 --> 00:18:24.620
With all the aggression it could channel through
its mannequin host, it gripped the Mask by

00:18:24.620 --> 00:18:27.010
the throat, his eyes bulging out of his head
again.

00:18:27.010 --> 00:18:31.660
“Gee, no need to get all choked up over
it,” he gagged.

00:18:31.660 --> 00:18:33.730
“You are so tiresome!”

00:18:33.730 --> 00:18:36.450
the Possessive Mask yelled, having finally
run out of patience.

00:18:36.450 --> 00:18:37.770
“You know what?

00:18:37.770 --> 00:18:42.700
I won’t merge with you; I should just kill
you and put an end to your buffoonery!

00:18:42.700 --> 00:18:47.559
Let me take this off you first though,”
its mannequin fingers started to hook into

00:18:47.559 --> 00:18:50.840
the mask’s seam at the back of his bald,
green head.

00:18:50.840 --> 00:18:51.840
“Wait, wait!”

00:18:51.840 --> 00:18:54.100
the Mask begged, putting both his hands up
in surrender.

00:18:54.100 --> 00:18:56.830
“At least give me a final request, huh?

00:18:56.830 --> 00:18:57.830
Mask to mask?”

00:18:57.830 --> 00:19:01.710
Before the Possessive Mask could respond,
the Mask had swept it off its dissolving mannequin

00:19:01.710 --> 00:19:02.710
feet.

00:19:02.710 --> 00:19:06.659
He started to spin it around in a wild, over
the top dance number, bopping and swinging

00:19:06.659 --> 00:19:09.440
to a tune that seemed to be coming from nowhere.

00:19:09.440 --> 00:19:14.920
The longer it went on for, the more and more
of SCP-035’s host body started to dissolve

00:19:14.920 --> 00:19:17.799
away, until the mannequin finally wasted away.

00:19:17.799 --> 00:19:22.659
All that was left was a bubbling pile of black
goo on the ground with the Possessive Mask

00:19:22.659 --> 00:19:24.160
laying in the middle.

00:19:24.160 --> 00:19:28.770
The Mask chuckled, noticing the fumes trailing
upwards into the air as the corrosive substance

00:19:28.770 --> 00:19:31.990
melted away the last of SCP-035 host.

00:19:31.990 --> 00:19:34.070
“Talk about sssmokin’!”

00:19:34.070 --> 00:19:39.680
Now go and check out “WHAT IF SCP-343 WORE
SCP-035?”

00:19:39.680 --> 00:19:40.680
and “The Whole Story!

00:19:40.680 --> 00:19:44.410
- What if SCP-096 Wore SCP-035?”

00:19:44.410 --> 00:19:46.700
for more adventures from the evil SCP-035!

